## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design low-latency multimodal inference on TF Serving, including shared encoders, caching, and batch policy.

## Key Concepts
- Multimodal architecture; dynamic batching; caching; TF-TRT; canary updates

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo config sketch
model_config_list {
  config {
    name: 'multimodal'
    dynamic_batching {
      max_batch_size: 64
      batch_queue_capacity: 128
      fbatch_timeout_micros: 50000
      num_batch_threads: 4
      allow_precision_loss: true
    }
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you measure tail latency and instrument per-queue metrics?
- How would you invalidate cached image embeddings when inputs change?

## Why This Is Asked
Assesses ability to design multi-tenant inference with dynamic schemas, deterministic preprocessing, and zero-downtime schema updates.

## Key Concepts
- Tenant-scoped schema registry with versioning
- Runtime feature alignment and type casting
- Per-tenant batching and routing to model versions
- Graceful schema hot-reload and in-flight request integrity
- gRPC path to TF Serving and error handling

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-code: load tenant schema and map fields to tensor order
function preprocess(input, tenantId, version){
  const schema = registry.get(tenantId, version);
  const ordered = schema.fields.map(f => input[f] ?? schema.defaults[f]);
  // cast types, handle missing, etc.
  return tf.tensor(ordered);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you monitor tail latency per-tenant and detect schema drift in this setup?
- What consistency model would you enforce for schema updates across replicas?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests practical TF.js deployment knowledge, including model conversion, quantization trade-offs, and browser inference pipelines.

## Key Concepts
- TensorFlow.js converter usage and quantization options
- Input/output shape alignment between Keras and tfjs graph model
- Static hosting of model.json and shard files
- Client-side preprocessing (224x224, [-1,1]) and top-k decoding

## Code Example
```javascript
// Load and infer with a TF.js GraphModel (illustrative)
const model = await tf.loadGraphModel('/models/mobilenetv2_web/model.json');
function preprocess(img) {
  const t = tf.browser.fromPixels(img).toFloat();
  const resized = tf.image.resizeBilinear(t, [224, 224]);
  const norm = resized.div(tf.scalar(127.5)).sub(tf.scalar(1));
  return norm.expandDims(0);
}
async function infer(img) {
  const input = preprocess(img);
  const logits = model.predict(input);
  const probs = logits.softmax ? logits.softmax() : logits;
  const data = await probs.data();
  const top3 = Array.from(data).map((p, i) => ({i, p}))
    .sort((a, b) => b.p - a.p)
    .slice(0, 3);
  return top3.map(x => x.i);
}
```
